# i18n content

## Config

- Default: `en` at `/`
- Others: `de` `/de`, `fr` `/fr`, `es` `/es`, `ja` `/ja`, `zh` `/zh` (`prefix_except_default`)
- `detectBrowserLanguage: false` — SSG-safe on GitHub Pages
- Switcher: `switchLocalePath()` so current route preserved

## Rules

1. Zero hardcoded user-facing strings in components — use `t('key')`.
2. Edit all six locale files in the same change. Keys must match.
3. Key nesting mirrors UI: `nav.*`, `hero.*`, `features.*`, `cta.*`, `footer.*`, `docsPage.*`, `impressum.*`, `meta.*`.
4. Docs article bodies live in `content/{locale}/*.md` — not in locale JSON. Translate all six folders together; keep slugs identical.
5. Interpolation: `{version}`, `{year}`, `{n}`, `{current}`, `{total}` — keep placeholders identical across locales.
6. Impressum TODO placeholders stay until owner supplies real legal data. Do not invent.

## Adding a string

1. Add key to `i18n/locales/en.json`
2. Add matching translations to `de.json`, `fr.json`, `es.json`, `ja.json`, `zh.json`
3. Consume via `const { t } = useI18n()` / `$t` in template
